# What the seeds of TestDifferential of the evaluator must reach: see stmttest.Reached.
# A line is the least number of the total of a kind over all seeds, a tab, and the kind.
# The numbers are written by hand, and a recount does not change them. They start from a third of
# the totals on 2026-11-25. A total below its number fails the test, and so does a kind that no
# seed reaches three times.
#
# A kind "x op y" is an operator whose operands were of the types x and y, with what it gave after
# the colon if it failed; "op with null" one with a NULL operand; "- of ..." a negation; "case: ..."
# the outcome of a whole case. A sum or a difference of an integer and a real cannot be infinite,
# nor a real divided by an integer, so those kinds are not here.
#
# The edges at the end: "x op y: exactly the largest integer" or "... smallest integer" is an
# integer result that is that bound; "x op y: subnormal, not zero" a real result below the
# smallest normal real that is not zero; "the smallest integer / a negative integer other than -1"
# a quotient of the smallest integer that fits; and "an error on the right of null" an operator
# whose left operand is NULL and whose right one fails, where SQLite gives NULL. A quotient that is
# exactly the largest integer and a real divided by an integer that is subnormal are too rare in
# the seeds to require. They start from a third of the totals on 2026-11-25, after the review.
